Fermix for Linux is two packages. `fermix` is the assistant itself, a background
service your own systemd runs. `fermix-desktop` is the window you set it up and
watch it from. The window depends on exactly the `fermix` version beside it, so
install the two together from this page.

{{ENGINE_NOTE}}

## Debian, Ubuntu, Mint, Pop!_OS, elementary

```sh
sudo apt install ./fermix_{{ENGINE_VERSION}}_$(dpkg --print-architecture).deb \
                 ./fermix-desktop_{{VERSION}}_$(dpkg --print-architecture).deb
```

## Fedora, RHEL, CentOS Stream, Alma, Rocky

```sh
sudo dnf install ./fermix-{{ENGINE_VERSION}}-1.$(uname -m).rpm \
                 ./fermix-desktop-{{VERSION}}-1.$(uname -m).rpm
```

## openSUSE and SLE

```sh
sudo zypper install ./fermix-{{ENGINE_VERSION}}-1.$(uname -m).rpm \
                    ./fermix-desktop-{{VERSION}}-1.$(uname -m).rpm
```

## Then

Open Fermix from your launcher and it will take you through setup. On a machine
with no desktop, run `fermix setup` in a terminal instead.

## Verifying what you downloaded

Every file on this page is signed with a keyless Sigstore certificate and carries
its own `.sha256`, `.sig` and `.pem` beside it. Name the file you downloaded and
check both:

```sh
package=fermix-desktop_{{VERSION}}_amd64.deb   # or the rpm, or the arm64 deb

sha256sum -c "$package.sha256"

cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate "$package.pem" \
  --signature "$package.sig" \
  --certificate-identity {{DESKTOP_IDENTITY}} \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  "$package"
```

{{ENGINE_SIGNING_NOTE}}

## Requirements

GTK 4.16 or later with libadwaita 1.6 or later. Both packages declare what they
need, so your package manager refuses the install on a host below that floor
rather than letting it fail when the window is opened.
